Fixes to part three:
-------------------------------

>VALKYRIE:
>   Special Abilities : Cold resistance

Stealth.

>ELF:
>   Special Abilities : Stealth, Speed

See invisible.  (And I'm not sure if they have stealth or not.)
>
>Potions :
>   You should almost never test out potions until you are at least seventh
>level, at full hit points and are on a cleared level. If you are not
>seventh level, you run the risk of wasting a potion of gain level.

No.  You want to drink your gain level potions at the first point where
gaining the level will allow you to use the CTRL-T (teleport) command
(provided you ate a L, N, t, or Q).  This is level 6 for Wizards, level
10 otherwise.  (I.e. if you have 1 potion drink it at level 9, or 5 for
Wizards).

>Wands :
>   ALWAYS test out wands as soon as there is a weak monster in your area
>to zap them at.

This is not a good idea.  Suppose you get polymorph and turn the weak
monster into a dragon?

If in Nethack; try engraving in a spot where there is some writing.  This
will identify a lot of wands; the rest can then be tried on a combination
of objects and monsters.  (The objects should include a corpse, for undead
turning, an an identified item with charges != 0, or plusses != 0, for
cancellation.)

>If I remember my hack folklore correctly, you take the same
>penalty for abandoning a dog as for killing him. -PG]

You don't.  Go ahead and abandon it.  It's perfectly safe.

>Carry extra items, but don't carry gold:

True, but...
>.... Since buying items is very rare, it is best to
>pile all the gold from a level next to the stairs going up. That way, on the
>way back up, the winning player can collect all the money he left behind.

No.  Weight for weight, the most valuable gem has more value than gold.
So you don't want to carry any gold at all out of the dungeon (unless you
want to use the bug that allows you to levitate up stairs even when overloaded.)

>   Do not believe that the only way a shapechanger can kill you is by
>turning into a cockatrice and stoning you. They also have the unique ability
>to swallow you, as a purple worm for instance, and then kill you by changing
>into a different creature. There is no defense against this attack other than
>to wear a ring of protection against shape changers. DO NOT take them lightly.

The reason this happened was due to a bug that got fixed with the introduction
of PC Hack 3.<something>, and the fix made it into Nethack.  You can no longer
die this way.

>Polymorphing wands:
>.... The best part is that the
>charges are the charges the old wand had, so that one wand may have up
>to 15 wishes!! Clearly this presents a simple, yet powerful (and cheap)
>method of winning. ...

Later Nethack versions fixed this, reducing the charges down to 3.

>
>[Polymorphing your dog:
>...One warning, though. If
>your dog turns into a dragon, he may still kill you with his breath
>weapon, if you get in his way. -PG]

No.  Tame monsters do not use breath weapons.

[I wouldn't have written it if it hadn't happened to me. Maybe that was
 only in version 1.4. Or maybe an un-tamed dragon snuck in and I thought
 it was my pet! -PG]
